WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.603
- I'm so excited you're here in person!

00:00:01.603 --> 00:00:04.394
- I know, finally!
- Okay, I'm very excited.

00:00:04.394 --> 00:00:05.950
I'm a lot. I'm a lot.
- We did it.

00:00:05.950 --> 00:00:07.490
So am I, so am I.

00:00:07.490 --> 00:00:08.417
- No, but I was so excited just

00:00:08.417 --> 00:00:09.690
to get to interview the last time.

00:00:09.690 --> 00:00:11.310
And I was like, "Oh my
God, she's in studio?

00:00:11.310 --> 00:00:12.340
I'm so excited."

00:00:12.340 --> 00:00:13.940
So you were in Europe
the last time, right?

00:00:13.940 --> 00:00:17.150
- Yes, yes, and now we
get a taste of normality

00:00:17.150 --> 00:00:19.210
and connectivity, I love it.
- Yeah!

00:00:19.210 --> 00:00:21.578
And actually see people in person.

00:00:21.578 --> 00:00:23.300
Well, last time, I think you live,

00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:25.460
is it London, Paris, like.
- Yes.

00:00:25.460 --> 00:00:26.740
- LA, you live everywhere.

00:00:26.740 --> 00:00:27.760
Where's the best food?

00:00:27.760 --> 00:00:31.130
- Oh, the best food.

00:00:31.130 --> 00:00:32.820
I got to tell you, the French are good.

00:00:32.820 --> 00:00:34.683
Not London. Sorry.

00:00:36.290 --> 00:00:38.200
- I love that I didn't even
ask you which one's worse

00:00:38.200 --> 00:00:39.790
and you were like, "I'm offering this up."

00:00:39.790 --> 00:00:40.623
- But you know what?

00:00:40.623 --> 00:00:43.101
They have some really
good international food.

00:00:43.101 --> 00:00:44.560
Like Indian food.
- I like Indian food.

00:00:44.560 --> 00:00:45.700
Yeah, Indian food there is good.

00:00:45.700 --> 00:00:47.170
- Yeah, but the French are good.

00:00:47.170 --> 00:00:49.276
- Yeah.
- Mexico is the best, but.

00:00:49.276 --> 00:00:52.036
(audience cheers)
- I love Mexican food.

00:00:52.036 --> 00:00:55.040
- You didn't put it in there.
- Yeah. I grew up in Texas.

00:00:55.040 --> 00:00:57.584
So I grew up with TexMex,
which is different, but.

00:00:57.584 --> 00:00:59.180
- We talked about it.
- We had authentic

00:00:59.180 --> 00:01:01.210
and we had TexMex, I like both.

00:01:01.210 --> 00:01:02.560
- Me too.
- But I will say,

00:01:02.560 --> 00:01:03.520
the last one we talked about it,

00:01:03.520 --> 00:01:05.520
it was tacos, you were
telling me the best tacos.

00:01:05.520 --> 00:01:07.350
Where are the best tacos in LA,

00:01:07.350 --> 00:01:08.600
if I wanted-
- My house.

00:01:10.538 --> 00:01:11.387
My house.
- Fine.

00:01:11.387 --> 00:01:14.334
I'll have to come taste them and hang out.

00:01:14.334 --> 00:01:16.740
- I get very creative with the tacos.

00:01:16.740 --> 00:01:19.170
- You love cooking?
- I love cooking,

00:01:19.170 --> 00:01:20.940
I love cooking Mexican food.

00:01:20.940 --> 00:01:23.660
And I love like, look at me.

00:01:23.660 --> 00:01:24.760
Do you know,

00:01:24.760 --> 00:01:28.870
I was going to that taco place
when I was like a little girl

00:01:28.870 --> 00:01:33.040
and my house is the second
best place for tacos.

00:01:33.040 --> 00:01:35.557
That place, (speaking foreign language)

00:01:35.557 --> 00:01:37.840
is the best cochinita tacos in the world.

00:01:37.840 --> 00:01:41.543
- You have the sexiest
voice on the planet.

00:01:43.600 --> 00:01:45.140
- You have to teach you how to sing.

00:01:45.140 --> 00:01:47.550
- Oh my God. If you can just, I tried.

00:01:47.550 --> 00:01:49.650
Even upstairs, I was trying
to have your like rasp

00:01:49.650 --> 00:01:51.830
and like your, and it's
just, it's so cool.

00:01:51.830 --> 00:01:53.920
Anyway.
- Just work really hard

00:01:53.920 --> 00:01:55.230
and don't sleep and you'll get to it

00:01:55.230 --> 00:01:57.360
when you're in your fifties.
- I do that and I still sound

00:01:57.360 --> 00:01:58.595
like a chipmunk.
- I'll come when you're

00:01:58.595 --> 00:02:00.500
in your fifties, trust me.

00:02:00.500 --> 00:02:02.330
- So wait, so wait, I didn't know this,

00:02:02.330 --> 00:02:04.650
but I saw the pictures and
I guess you posted them.

00:02:04.650 --> 00:02:07.860
You met Eminem, but you
accidentally spilled water on him?

00:02:07.860 --> 00:02:09.060
How did that happen?

00:02:09.060 --> 00:02:10.060
- Oh my God.

00:02:10.060 --> 00:02:12.200
You see people don't,

00:02:12.200 --> 00:02:13.870
I don't look like this happens to me,

00:02:13.870 --> 00:02:15.970
but I have terrible stage fright.

00:02:15.970 --> 00:02:16.920
- Oh!
- I'm just a really

00:02:16.920 --> 00:02:19.270
good actress that I pretend
- Oh my gosh, you are.

00:02:19.270 --> 00:02:22.860
- It's not happening, but
I really get it very bad.

00:02:22.860 --> 00:02:26.060
Like I go just, my mouth gets dry.

00:02:26.060 --> 00:02:28.624
And so I have a song

00:02:28.624 --> 00:02:32.883
that I put in my head that
helps me get through it.

00:02:33.923 --> 00:02:35.217
Which is-
- Please say it's Eminem.

00:02:35.217 --> 00:02:36.117
- "Lose Yourself."

00:02:37.103 --> 00:02:40.250
I mean, you hear that, you
feel like you can do anything,

00:02:40.250 --> 00:02:41.210
right?
- That's true. That's true.

00:02:41.210 --> 00:02:43.220
- So I hear it in my head.

00:02:43.220 --> 00:02:46.400
And I was going to present at the Oscars,

00:02:46.400 --> 00:02:48.600
which is really nerve wracking,

00:02:48.600 --> 00:02:50.350
especially if you have stage fright.

00:02:50.350 --> 00:02:51.340
- But when you're you,

00:02:51.340 --> 00:02:53.430
that's crazy!
- I went like this, you know?

00:02:53.430 --> 00:02:55.610
I could see my hearts coming.
- If I were you for one day,

00:02:55.610 --> 00:02:57.040
I would never be nervous.
- Oh no!

00:02:57.040 --> 00:02:59.869
I'm like, and then I come out like, "Hi!"

00:02:59.869 --> 00:03:01.510
But I'm dying inside!

00:03:01.510 --> 00:03:03.883
- You're a great actor!
- Yes, I am!

00:03:05.050 --> 00:03:07.807
They should give me an
Oscar just for presenting

00:03:07.807 --> 00:03:09.527
at the Oscars.

00:03:09.527 --> 00:03:12.380
Just for presenting.
- That was a great acting job.

00:03:12.380 --> 00:03:14.043
- And this one day, I was extra nervous

00:03:14.043 --> 00:03:16.860
because I hadn't slept, I was jet lagged,

00:03:16.860 --> 00:03:18.374
I was feeling shaky.

00:03:18.374 --> 00:03:21.730
And so, this one time,
I'm drinking the water

00:03:21.730 --> 00:03:23.560
because my mouth immediately goes dry.

00:03:23.560 --> 00:03:26.050
- Yeah.
- Even with the water.

00:03:26.050 --> 00:03:28.640
And I am thinking, I'm walking towards it,

00:03:28.640 --> 00:03:32.570
in my head, thinking,
"Lose Yourself," you know.

00:03:32.570 --> 00:03:34.960
I'm singing the song in my head.

00:03:34.960 --> 00:03:38.010
And then I kind of feel like it's not

00:03:38.010 --> 00:03:39.840
syncing to something.

00:03:39.840 --> 00:03:43.210
And I am like drinking the water

00:03:43.210 --> 00:03:44.093
and then I go,

00:03:45.620 --> 00:03:46.453
wait a minute,

00:03:47.700 --> 00:03:49.270
have I lost it?

00:03:49.270 --> 00:03:53.491
I go to the person, "Is 'Lose
Yourself' playing right now?"

00:03:53.491 --> 00:03:55.710
Because I heard it like in a stereo,

00:03:55.710 --> 00:03:58.660
but he was not announced that
he was gonna be at the Oscars.

00:03:58.660 --> 00:04:01.080
- Oh!
- As I was ready to come out,

00:04:01.080 --> 00:04:03.310
he was on stage playing "Lose Yourself,"

00:04:03.310 --> 00:04:05.040
but I didn't know.
- And surprised it.

00:04:05.040 --> 00:04:06.800
- I knew everybody that was at the Oscars,

00:04:06.800 --> 00:04:08.030
this was a surprise.

00:04:08.030 --> 00:04:10.610
And so I am so nervous
that I think it's me

00:04:10.610 --> 00:04:12.803
and then all of a sudden, wait a minute?

00:04:13.640 --> 00:04:14.670
It was really scary

00:04:14.670 --> 00:04:15.600
by the way.
- Wouldn't it have been great

00:04:15.600 --> 00:04:17.443
though if everyone would have
been like, "I don't know what

00:04:17.443 --> 00:04:18.901
you're talking about."
- No, I know!

00:04:18.901 --> 00:04:21.080
- "I don't hear a thing."
- I was actually embarrassed

00:04:21.080 --> 00:04:24.800
to ask, I hesitated for a
minute and it was the end of it.

00:04:24.800 --> 00:04:27.500
And in this moment I'm like more nervous

00:04:27.500 --> 00:04:30.920
and he comes out exactly
on the side that I am in.

00:04:30.920 --> 00:04:34.350
And I just, I'm so nervous, I
go, "I love you! I love you!"

00:04:34.350 --> 00:04:36.060
- You're shaking the water.

00:04:36.060 --> 00:04:37.363
- I spit it out.

00:04:38.890 --> 00:04:41.527
I was, I drank, and I said,
"I love you! I love you!"

00:04:42.900 --> 00:04:44.669
- That goes so much worse!

00:04:44.669 --> 00:04:46.950
Oh my God! Oh my God!
- I know!

00:04:46.950 --> 00:04:48.750
And then I see that he's like,

00:04:48.750 --> 00:04:51.329
in shock with water all over and I go,

00:04:51.329 --> 00:04:54.551
- First of all.
- "I'm sorry! I'm sorry!"

00:04:54.551 --> 00:04:56.163
And they're like, "Go! Go!"

00:04:56.163 --> 00:04:57.565
"I'm sorry!"

00:04:57.565 --> 00:04:59.148
And then they, they "Go, go!"

00:04:59.148 --> 00:05:02.202
And I just, "Somebody take a picture!"

00:05:02.202 --> 00:05:04.390
They took a picture and then I left.

00:05:04.390 --> 00:05:07.823
- You both look terrified.
- I feel so humiliated.

00:05:07.823 --> 00:05:09.620
I still had to go and do it

00:05:09.620 --> 00:05:13.030
and the next day I went
home and I said, "Oh my God.

00:05:13.030 --> 00:05:15.407
My hero thinks I'm a freak."

00:05:15.407 --> 00:05:19.890
And the next morning they asked him,

00:05:19.890 --> 00:05:22.098
because it was a big
deal, it was a surprise.

00:05:22.098 --> 00:05:24.220
"Hey, did you enjoy going this time?"

00:05:24.220 --> 00:05:27.110
Because when he won for
that song, he didn't go.

00:05:27.110 --> 00:05:29.077
And he said something like,

00:05:29.077 --> 00:05:32.980
"Oh, I really enjoyed it because
I got to meet Salma Hayek."

00:05:32.980 --> 00:05:36.147
- Yeah, yeah! It was so cool.
(audience cheers)

00:05:36.147 --> 00:05:37.315
I don't know if you know this,

00:05:37.315 --> 00:05:39.557
but like a lot of people like you.

00:05:39.557 --> 00:05:42.622
- But I spit on him!
- Kind of a big deal. Yeah.

00:05:42.622 --> 00:05:44.910
You kind of might be an even
bigger deal than Eminem, so.

00:05:44.910 --> 00:05:46.250
And I love Eminem.
- Well maybe,

00:05:46.250 --> 00:05:48.200
he really looked very terrified.

00:05:48.200 --> 00:05:50.453
- [Kelly] He did look
terrified, it's awesome.

